-book/tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-preproof-review-20261011/fresh-independent-preproof-context-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256_before\": \"fe427b8f397edd570e8c5f7960c7d0a35fbf8465f10b3b8d35fb27636be2eb4c\",\n+      \"bytes\": 12758,\n+      \"sha256_after\": \"fe427b8f397edd570e8c5f7960c7d0a35fbf8465f10b3b8d35fb27636be2eb4c\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"E:/ABRL/worktrees/research-online-book/tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-body-authorization-20261011/parent-authorization-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256_before\": \"d2ddf2ec4aa1aba8186125b6dcbf81e9d8fa3155c9cfbb21eab323ab1197db29\",\n+      \"bytes\": 1655,\n+      \"sha256_after\": \"d2ddf2ec4aa1aba8186125b6dcbf81e9d8fa3155c9cfbb21eab323ab1197db29\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"inputs_unchanged_before_after\": true\n+}"},{"sha":"8e68df14f1384d33d3950af1f89f63ee8e5f1d8a","filename":"runs/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011/independent-production-body/fresh-production-body-review-v1.md","status":"added","additions":7,"deletions":0,"changes":7,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-production-body%2Ffresh-production-body-review-v1.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-production-body%2Ffresh-production-body-review-v1.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-production-body%2Ffresh-production-body-review-v1.md?ref=c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@\n+Independent production BODY review: accepted-local-candidate; blocking repairs: none.\n+\n+The sole frozen finite_regret_identity theorem retains its exact full header and hT. Its cumulative recurrence and induction prove the finite-real telescope for arbitrary signed regularizers/losses and arbitrary terminal splice, retaining both drift and the positive terminal gap. No optimizer or desired conclusion premise is introduced.\n+\n+All 54 v2 manifest rows and the complete artifact set were checked; all 1220 preproof inputs remain unchanged. Actual focused, compiled public import and full proof print succeed, with only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. The full successful raw print is 20,815,000 bytes. V2 corrects Nat.rec to the actual direct VALUE occurrence Nat.recAux; old report and all three failed attempts remain preserved. Occurrence evidence is not a necessity or transitive graph claim.\n+\n+This accepts one local algebra candidate only. Canary and combined root/Tests/harness/site gates remain pending. Whole Eq7.47/15.31, EReal/attainment/producer obligations, B4, seven containers, six future claims and Goal remain open. No native whole-loop, chapter, merge or publication acceptance. Requested GPT-6 Astra / medium; runtime not independently attested."},{"sha":"8ba068699c3c24fc43b5595f4d39b0478cf70025","filename":"runs/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011/independent-source-topology/fresh-independent-source-topology-review-v1.json","status":"added","additions":138,"deletions":0,"changes":138,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v1.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v1.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v1.json?ref=c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@\n+{\n+  \"utc\": \"2026-10-11T07:39:03.684576+00:00\",\n+  \"actor\": \"/root/adaptive_reviewer\",\n+  \"requested_model_effort\": \"GPT-6 Astra / medium; runtime not attested\",\n+  \"verdict\": \"repair-before-source-topology-acceptance\",\n+  \"header_verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta finite algebra header only\",\n+  \"proposal_sha256\": \"1338aa71bb80ab820b89f77d8f3e4e50dd9f9d0cdf05b16471859aaadc83e24f\",\n+  \"header_sha256\": \"92e0dcfac53595e35b68bfd8083c09640d06da809355ab02ec4eb4b007b0bd67\",\n+  \"inputs_before\": [\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/topology-proposal-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"1338aa71bb80ab820b89f77d8f3e4e50dd9f9d0cdf05b16471859aaadc83e24f\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/source-header-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"adda7e17c6ebf0ba1b8c24d9cd78e0df763f55000521ec01fb8d94b51229228f\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/fresh-blind-binding-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"0e0362c318b73877cb4d7fa1ce5294d33b56baa71d5ff2f73613722d7aa3be6e\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-proposal-20261011/header-proposal-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"7a5848efbf57ba9c76c987baae75856331100325fc4c9130ead409b5ba3815fb\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-proposal-20261011/neutral-proposed-header-v1.txt\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"92e0dcfac53595e35b68bfd8083c09640d06da809355ab02ec4eb4b007b0bd67\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-blind-20261011/fresh-blind-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"a76cbbfc57db5d4f9107574d2167435c06ad7bcb980e5a50554a8f8508e551bc\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"source_pdf\": {\n+    \"path\": \"E:\\\\ABRL\\\\worktrees\\\\research-online-ogd\\\\tmp\\\\pdfs\\\\orabona-v10.pdf\",\n+    \"sha256\": \"cef4edfa97a6e063e53e9c532717c50aa156e5bc782ea49f969b3385011a1b17\"\n+  },\n+  \"original_pixels\": [\n+    {\n+      \"pdf_page\": 141,\n+      \"printed_page\": 129,\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-lookahead-terminal-independent-review-20261011/page-141.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"5e84c10fca956ac5f61c577176da994d122e0aa4381547bf98b1af07d781dd96\",\n+      \"personally_viewed\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"pdf_page\": 142,\n+      \"printed_page\": 130,\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-lookahead-terminal-independent-review-20261011/page-142.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"5c3589b9716f50adf599b796a6988cf7f5d711684801ca9105c1670acd58b8ea\",\n+      \"personally_viewed\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"pdf_page\": 278,\n+      \"printed_page\": 266,\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-lookahead-terminal-independent-review-20261011/page-278.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"5fa1dea63493c7f7c6e198ea0a4daddf4c61cf8c0d65f7d2ee614e8270ace710\",\n+      \"personally_viewed\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"pdf_page\": 279,\n+      \"printed_page\": 267,\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-lookahead-terminal-independent-review-20261011/page-279.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"b36cc73854971400a96fd6b5c68140a905efb4958e3142de6f80ed1440abce13\",\n+      \"personally_viewed\": true\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"independent_source_reading\": \"Personally read original pixels first, then the decoder source/header verdict. No new production BODY, snapshot or VALUE read; no BODY exists or compilation inferred.\",\n+  \"seven_slots\": {\n+    \"objects\": \"Arbitrary E; total real psi/loss; arbitrary x,u,z; natural positive T.\",\n+    \"quantifiers\": \"Universal functions and states, no feasible-set or optimizer requirement.\",\n+    \"hypotheses\": \"Only hT propositional; finite real arithmetic is an explicit specialization of extended source, not finiteness discharge.\",\n+    \"conclusion\": \"Exact finite regret equality, not bound or actual algorithm trajectory.\",\n+    \"constants\": \"All coefficients plus/minus1; no lambda/half/Young performance factor claimed.\",\n+    \"indexing\": \"Source s=1..T maps leaf t=s-1; inclusive G_t has losses0..t; y changes exactly coordinateT; interior drift t=0..T-2; terminal G_(T-1).\",\n+    \"boundary\": \"T1 drift empty; z cancels algebraically across last movement and positive gap, but gap cannot separately be discarded. T0 excluded and unrestricted version false.\"\n+  },\n+  \"independent_algebra_check\": \"For t>=1, G_t(y_t)-G_(t-1)(y_t)=loss_t(y_t)+psi_t(y_t)-psi_(t-1)(y_t). Summing cancels adjacent potentials, leaving initial psi0, terminal G_(T-1), and exactly the displayed interior drift. Add comparator identity G_(T-1)(u)=psi_(T-1)(u)+sum losses(u). This is ordinary mathematical review, not Lean BODY or kernel validation.\",\n+  \"counterevidence_check\": \"T1 psi=v^2/2, loss=hint=(v-1)^2/2, x=u=1/2, repeated-hint terminal z=2/3, lambda2: regret0, printed sharp RHS-1/36, finite gap+1/36. Rational values independently checked; no Lean counterexample claimed.\",\n+  \"blocking_repairs\": [\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"T1\",\n+      \"location\": \"nodes/excluded and source edges\",\n+      \"repair\": \"Add explicit dispositions for Theorem7.47 real-round existence/uniqueness and FTRL reinterpretation psi+hint with Lemma7.5/Theorem6.9; Lemma7.1 comparator-gap discard and initial-minimum substitution/hint telescoping; PDF141 prediction-generation/no-assumption and perfect-hint motivation paragraphs; PDF278 BTRL=optimistic FTRL with hint=loss and psi=0 BTL specialization; PDF279 absence of nonnegative gradient terms. These may be context/excluded-from-leaf with owning targets retained, but not absent. Record analytic qualification as OPEN, not automatically valid from citations.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"T2\",\n+      \"location\": \"edges[1],edges[2],edges[3] and source-bound nodes\",\n+      \"repair\": \"Keep literal SRC-7.47-SHARP and SRC-15.31 as immutable source claims. Add distinct labeled corrected endpoint nodes and retarget corrected AND edges to them. Declare the current dangling future corrected Young endpoint as a node with explicit remaining/open status. Distinguish source derivation/reinterpretation edges from proposed corrected-route edges; no verified route implied.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"T3\",\n+      \"location\": \"OPEN-GHOST and OPEN-BTRL claims\",\n+      \"repair\": \"Eliminate mixed index ambiguity: explicitly state source one-based terminal objective G_T equals leaf G_(T-1); BTRL repeated last played state source x_T equals leaf x(T-1), spliced y(T)=z. Leaf G_T/x(T) would instead include an extra loss or unused state. Preserve zero-hint attained finite-minimizer qualification and no gap-sign assumption on arbitrary z.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"T4\",\n+      \"location\": \"SRC-TERMINAL-REPEAT\",\n+      \"repair\": \"Separate legitimate virtual repeat choices from invalid claimed cancellation. Repeating final hint/regularizer leaves scored rounds unchanged; it does not itself refute anything. The unsupported cancellation omits hint_T(u)-hint_T(x_(T+1)); classify only witnessed sharp completion/cancellation as invalid, not all terminal repetition or Young alternatives.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"positive_findings\": [\n+    \"17 proposed nodes and4 exclusions retain main literal bounds and terminal correction intent.\",\n+    \"Finite-real leaf is properly separated from EReal support/finiteness, actual minimizers, stability and Young obligations.\",\n+    \"All current correction joins are AND; no BODY/actual proof dependency or verified alternative route asserted.\",\n+    \"Negative movement alone does not justify dropping arbitrary terminal gap; full corrected7.47/15.31 remain OPEN.\",\n+    \"Fresh blind header reconstruction agrees on seven slots, T1/T0 and unused x(T); source-exposed decoder not mislabeled blind.\"\n+  ],\n+  \"scope\": \"No header mutation requested. No freeze/BODY authorization, full B4 closure, prescient delivery/chapter acceptance, Goal completion, canonical or Git writes. All7containers+6futureclaims remain required/open.\",\n+  \"inputs_after\": [\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/topology-proposal-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"1338aa71bb80ab820b89f77d8f3e4e50dd9f9d0cdf05b16471859aaadc83e24f\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/source-header-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"adda7e17c6ebf0ba1b8c24d9cd78e0df763f55000521ec01fb8d94b51229228f\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/fresh-blind-binding-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"0e0362c318b73877cb4d7fa1ce5294d33b56baa71d5ff2f73613722d7aa3be6e\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-proposal-20261011/header-proposal-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"7a5848efbf57ba9c76c987baae75856331100325fc4c9130ead409b5ba3815fb\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-proposal-20261011/neutral-proposed-header-v1.txt\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"92e0dcfac53595e35b68bfd8083c09640d06da809355ab02ec4eb4b007b0bd67\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-blind-20261011/fresh-blind-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"a76cbbfc57db5d4f9107574d2167435c06ad7bcb980e5a50554a8f8508e551bc\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"inputs_unchanged\": true\n+}"},{"sha":"cad84f9846dc98b657ae2249e22096e992ce254c","filename":"runs/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011/independent-source-topology/fresh-independent-source-topology-review-v1.md","status":"added","additions":5,"deletions":0,"changes":5,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v1.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v1.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v1.md?ref=c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+Finite algebra HEADER accepted with explicit finite-real/arbitrary-carrier delta; topology requires four bounded repairs.\n+\n+T1: explicitly dispose of source existence/uniqueness, Lemma7.1/hint cancellation and substantive optimistic/BTRL specialization paragraphs. T2: distinguish corrected endpoint nodes from literal source nodes and declare Young output. T3: resolve source G_T/x_T versus leaf G_(T-1)/x(T-1) indexing. T4: mark invalid cancellation/sharp completion, not the legitimate virtual repeat operation itself.\n+\n+Personally inspected original PDF141/142/278/279 pixels. Arbitrary z and positive terminal gap, interior drift and T>0 are faithful to the labeled finite identity; no full source-bound or BODY acceptance."},{"sha":"efdbcd70cf72e60977b69495dbff302e9f7675d0","filename":"runs/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011/independent-source-topology/fresh-independent-source-topology-review-v2.json","status":"added","additions":116,"deletions":0,"changes":116,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v2.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v2.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v2.json?ref=c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@\n+{\n+  \"utc\": \"2026-10-11T07:50:30.563912+00:00\",\n+  \"actor\": \"/root/adaptive_reviewer\",\n+  \"requested_model_effort\": \"GPT-6 Astra / medium; runtime not attested\",\n+  \"verdict\": \"accepted-with-explicit-delta-source-topology-only\",\n+  \"blocking_repairs\": [],\n+  \"approved_proposal_sha256\": \"d7d6051f3788797b53a19d5d80f163bdca80491281ec13be998b4c2d106ad8bc\",\n+  \"approved_header_sha256\": \"92e0dcfac53595e35b68bfd8083c09640d06da809355ab02ec4eb4b007b0bd67\",\n+  \"inputs_before\": [\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/topology-proposal-v2.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"d7d6051f3788797b53a19d5d80f163bdca80491281ec13be998b4c2d106ad8bc\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/topology-proposal-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"1338aa71bb80ab820b89f77d8f3e4e50dd9f9d0cdf05b16471859aaadc83e24f\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-topology-review-20261011/fresh-independent-source-topology-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"701e22c6dfe28a7e5bfd7f1c83a96dadb0af411867947ff35e3d65f76d242d7b\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-proposal-20261011/neutral-proposed-header-v1.txt\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"92e0dcfac53595e35b68bfd8083c09640d06da809355ab02ec4eb4b007b0bd67\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-blind-20261011/fresh-blind-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"a76cbbfc57db5d4f9107574d2167435c06ad7bcb980e5a50554a8f8508e551bc\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/source-header-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"adda7e17c6ebf0ba1b8c24d9cd78e0df763f55000521ec01fb8d94b51229228f\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"inputs_after\": [\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/topology-proposal-v2.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"d7d6051f3788797b53a19d5d80f163bdca80491281ec13be998b4c2d106ad8bc\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/topology-proposal-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"1338aa71bb80ab820b89f77d8f3e4e50dd9f9d0cdf05b16471859aaadc83e24f\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-topology-review-20261011/fresh-independent-source-topology-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"701e22c6dfe28a7e5bfd7f1c83a96dadb0af411867947ff35e3d65f76d242d7b\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-proposal-20261011/neutral-proposed-header-v1.txt\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"92e0dcfac53595e35b68bfd8083c09640d06da809355ab02ec4eb4b007b0bd67\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-blind-20261011/fresh-blind-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"a76cbbfc57db5d4f9107574d2167435c06ad7bcb980e5a50554a8f8508e551bc\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-source-review-20261011/source-header-review-v1.json\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"adda7e17c6ebf0ba1b8c24d9cd78e0df763f55000521ec01fb8d94b51229228f\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"inputs_unchanged\": true,\n+  \"source_pixels\": [\n+    {\n+      \"pdf_page\": 141,\n+      \"printed_page\": 129,\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-lookahead-terminal-independent-review-20261011/page-141.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"5e84c10fca956ac5f61c577176da994d122e0aa4381547bf98b1af07d781dd96\",\n+      \"personally_viewed\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"pdf_page\": 142,\n+      \"printed_page\": 130,\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-lookahead-terminal-independent-review-20261011/page-142.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"5c3589b9716f50adf599b796a6988cf7f5d711684801ca9105c1670acd58b8ea\",\n+      \"personally_viewed\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"pdf_page\": 278,\n+      \"printed_page\": 266,\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-lookahead-terminal-independent-review-20261011/page-278.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"5fa1dea63493c7f7c6e198ea0a4daddf4c61cf8c0d65f7d2ee614e8270ace710\",\n+      \"personally_viewed\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"pdf_page\": 279,\n+      \"printed_page\": 267,\n+      \"path\": \"tmp/online-lookahead-terminal-independent-review-20261011/page-279.png\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"b36cc73854971400a96fd6b5c68140a905efb4958e3142de6f80ed1440abce13\",\n+      \"personally_viewed\": true\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"pixel_review_boundary\": \"All four original PDF141/142/278/279 pixels personally viewed in immediately preceding v1 review; their exact bytes and pinned PDF hash reverified now. No redundant viewing tool call claimed.\",\n+  \"source_pdf\": {\n+    \"path\": \"E:\\\\ABRL\\\\worktrees\\\\research-online-ogd\\\\tmp\\\\pdfs\\\\orabona-v10.pdf\",\n+    \"sha256\": \"cef4edfa97a6e063e53e9c532717c50aa156e5bc782ea49f969b3385011a1b17\"\n+  },\n+  \"T1\": \"Resolved. Nine source-context/claim additions explicitly dispose of arbitrary-hint motivation, FTRL reinterpretation, actual existence/uniqueness citation, Lemma7.1 hinted gap, initial minimum/hint telescoping, perfect-hint BTRL, zero-regularizer BTL, and gradient-absence interpretation. Analytic qualification and owning-chapter results remain OPEN; explicit EXCLUDED_FROM_FINITE_LEAF is not deletion.\",\n+  \"T2\": \"Resolved. Three distinct CORRECTED endpoint IDs receive unverified AND edges. Original printed sharp/BTRL claims retain claim bytes. No dangling output. Separate S1-S7 edges describe source narrative including invalid cancellation, not valid implication or compiled dependency.\",\n+  \"T3\": \"Resolved. Explicit one-based/source versus zero-based/leaf map binds sourceG_T=leafG(T-1), last sourcex_T=leafx(T-1), terminaly(T)=z; unused leafx(T) and extra loss in leafG(T) are explicitly excluded. Ghost attained minimum/finiteness and arbitrary-z gap-sign boundary remain.\",\n+  \"T4\": \"Resolved. Virtual repetition is legitimate for preserving real rounds. Distinct invalid-cancellation node retains hint_(T+1)(u)-hint_(T+1)(z), the bounded repeated-hint T1 sharp witness, and explicitly avoids blanket refutation of algorithms, repaired or Young endpoints. SOURCE_INVALID here is ordinary source-counterevidence, not a new Lean proof.\",\n+  \"structural_checks\": {\n+    \"old_node_ids_retained\": 17,\n+    \"new_node_ids\": 12,\n+    \"total_nodes\": 29,\n+    \"old_exclusion_objects_exact\": 4,\n+    \"all_claim_fingerprints_valid\": true,\n+    \"all_edge_endpoints_declared\": true,\n+    \"all_edges_unverified\": true,\n+    \"header_unchanged\": true,\n+    \"fresh_blind_hash_verified\": true\n+  },\n+  \"mathematical_scope\": \"Finite-real arbitrary-carrier exact identity only: positive horizon, same played prefix, inclusive cumulative G, interior regularizer drift and positive terminal gap. All full EReal adapters, qualified support/strong-convexity, existence/attainment, actual producer and corrected7.47/15.31 sharp/Young endpoints remain separate mandatory obligations. No true-algorithm recurrence premise or desired regret premise added to leaf.\",\n+  \"source_correction_status\": \"Topology approves organization and explicit qualification of pending corrected targets; it does not accept full corrected endpoint theorems or silently replace original source.\",\n+  \"exposure\": \"No new B4 production BODY/snapshot/TYPEVALUE read; no build, freeze, proof authorization, gate execution, canonical source or RUN mutation.\",\n+  \"remaining_boundary\": \"All7containers+6futureclaims and B4 endpoints mandatory/open; C2partial/null and GoalACTIVE unchanged.\"\n+}"},{"sha":"269c83a3f9608698e77e9220abb1fe8381ad8ecc","filename":"runs/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011/independent-source-topology/fresh-independent-source-topology-review-v2.md","status":"added","additions":3,"deletions":0,"changes":3,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v2.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v2.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-source-topology%2Ffresh-independent-source-topology-review-v2.md?ref=c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Accepted source-only topology v2 with explicit correction boundaries; no blocking repairs. T1-T4 resolved: substantive source steps explicitly disposed, corrected endpoints have distinct declared nodes, source/leaf terminal indices are mapped, and invalid cancellation is separated from legitimate virtual repetition. All17old IDs and4exclusion objects retained,12nodes added;29claim hashes and all unverified edge endpoints checked.\n+\n+The unchanged finite-real identity header and fresh blind reconstruction remain bound. Four previously personally viewed original source pixels and PDF bytes rehashed. Full EReal/analytic/attainment/producer/7.47/15.31 obligations remain mandatory OPEN. No freeze, BODY, compiler, chapter or Goal acceptance."},{"sha":"adcc275c248edcc659afd838a7195b5a6fe485eb","filename":"runs/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011/independent-stabilization/.gitattributes","status":"added","additions":3,"deletions":0,"changes":3,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Findependent-stabilization%2F.gitattributes","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/c445c93